From 92d81694c53aec5f9ca6dd987015934cfc958c15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:35:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dicts: name the socket bind shim on the Tweaks page

RTWK_03 read "nvram netlink workaround", which describes the symptom but never
names the mechanism. The control has existed since ef5078d35a and has defaulted
to ON since the same commit, but nothing on the page identifies it as the
socket bind shim - so the setting is present and correct while reading as
absent to the person looking for it. That is a discoverability defect, not a
missing feature, and it was raised as "the bind fix needs a toggle" twice.

  RTWK_03  Socket bind shim (nvram netlink)
  RTWK_04  ... adds "On by default", since the default is the other half of
           what was being asked, and the page was the only place that could
           have answered it.

Value-only rewrite in all 25 packs: keys, key order and line counts are
untouched, lockstep holds at 6635. Rule 29 checked - neither value contains a
quote or apostrophe, and both render in HTML text context.

English-seeded in all 25 as usual; the 24 non-English packs now carry English
for these two keys and are owed a translation pass.

Staged with the [A-Z][A-Z].dict pathspec, not *.dict: the glob catches the
gitignored temp.dict and aborts the whole add.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
